      "problem": "$6x+(3x+5)\\cdot (-6)=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we distribute the $(-6)$ over each of the terms in parentheses.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}6x+(3x+5)\\cdot (-6) & = \\\\ 6x+3x\\cdot (-6)+5\\cdot (-6) & = \\\\ 6x+(-18x)+(-30) & = \\\\ 6x-18x-30\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we collect like terms.\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-18x-30 & = \\\\ (6x-18x)-30 & = \\\\ -12x-30 & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
